WEBVTT

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:14.780
We've done our best to stop the violence in the villages, but we can only do so much.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.950
We can hope to be a stopgap at best.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.380
The kingdom will need to step up and do something.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:24.410
But what can they hope to accomplish without a king?

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:31.120
The castle! It's the capital!

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.860
We finally made it!

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:40.870
I'm back...

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:56.890
<i>In the city without love</i> <i>only your smile remains.</i>

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:06.890
<i>Hold me tight to crush the loneliness,</i> <i>it's all that stops these pains.</i>

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:17.270
<i>You're constrained by that limit.</i>
<i>Free yourself and break apart the chains.</i>

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:27.270
<i>It's all gonna burn on down.</i>
<i>Dance to the flames that consume the night.</i>

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:37.450
<i>The inferno rages on. It's almost</i> <i>as beautiful as you. Beautiful and bright.</i>

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:47.970
<i>Dance to the end of the night.</i>

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:57.970
<i>The inferno rages on. It's almost</i> <i>as beautiful as you. Beautiful and bright. Dance!</i>

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:08.650
<i>In the city without love</i>

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:46.030
What's the point of keeping a castle with no master?

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:49.060
I'm sure Prince Emilio is alive and well.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:51.900
We still don't even know how the king died.

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:56.370
H-He's back!

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:57.410
Aaron?

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:01.430
Prince Emilio... He's returned to the castle!

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:06.550
"17: Return"

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:23.470
We're back!

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:26.070
This castle sure is amazing!

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:28.540
You've seen it once already.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:32.270
Back then, I was too busy running away to notice anything.

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:34.610
It's unusually quiet though.

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:37.650
And I can only sense a few people.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.880
Prince Emilio!

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:40.370
Thank goodness you're safe!

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:45.050
Prince Emilio, welcome back.

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:47.320
You two... So much has changed.

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:49.120
But we're the same as always.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:50.660
Alicia came, too...

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:53.600
I'm sorry for going missing for so long.

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:58.000
It's okay, as long as you're safe and sound.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.490
What a nice little reunion this is.

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:03.840
Prince Emilio!

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:05.140
Aaron!

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:07.940
I'm glad to see you well, Prince Emilio.

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:10.180
We've been eagerly awaiting your return.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:13.120
Yes, it's good to see you, too.

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:15.740
By the way, who are these others?

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:21.150
They're comrades I've made on my journey.

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:29.600
Over half the soldiers never returned from the king's pilgrimage.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:30.970
Half?!

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:33.170
But there were barely any casualties.

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:35.040
That may be true, however...

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.140
The others deserted?

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:43.510
I'm sure they foresaw the chaos and decided it better to become brigands instead.

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:45.480
I can't believe it!

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:48.520
The capital is in disorder and so many have left the castle.

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:54.690
The few who remain did so hoping for your eventual return.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:56.660
What do you think you're doing?!

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:00.060
Who gave you permission to be here?

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:03.070
I won't have anyone spying around the castle!

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:05.000
Have a problem with us?

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:11.500
A problem? I don't know who you think you are, but the safety of this castle comes first.

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:19.680
Enough!

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:20.880
Prince Emilio!

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:22.920
What, get in another fight?

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:24.590
What happened here?

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:27.760
These people threatened us for no reason.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.490
I can only assume they are up to no good when I find

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:34.400
people wandering around the halls of the castle.

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:41.900
These are comrades of mine. They mean no harm.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:42.740
But...

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:44.070
Put down your sword.

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:46.610
Very well.

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:49.040
If that is your command.

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:53.270
You guys put your weapons away, too.

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:58.220
Forgive me. When strangers start roaming the halls, we...

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:03.730
I know. You're just trying to ensure my safety as best you can.

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:11.200
Please have the Zoozians or anyone we don't know refrain from wandering the halls.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:12.600
Excuse us.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:20.640
That guy seems like a hardhead.

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:26.080
But after seeing that, I'm almost starting to believe you're really a prince.

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:28.320
Prince Em-i-li-o.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:29.790
Quit it.

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:31.990
It gives me the chills when you call me prince.

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:32.980
Wha--?

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:36.990
Prince, huh?

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:41.650
No one's here...

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:48.940
No one thinks it's worth doing research when the capital is falling apart.

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:53.340
As long as we have curious minds, it's always worth researching something!

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:56.150
That's what makes science so great!

00:06:56.150 --> 00:06:58.280
Isn't that right, professor?

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:00.250
Yes, very true.

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:03.090
Now, let's get started with our analysis.

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:03.790
Sure!

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:06.120
Some things just never change.

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:11.130
Oh! Looks like Rodney came, too!

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:17.200
Yeah, but I'm not even close to a researcher now.
I just run a bread shop, remember?

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:20.040
I can't believe you pulled me out of retirement for this.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:24.170
If Endora is destroyed, you won't get to bake your bread anymore.

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:25.300
I suppose not.

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:27.810
This is...?

00:07:27.810 --> 00:07:30.880
My senior back when I was in research.

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:35.150
A scientist whose achievements are countless and worthy of much respect.

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:40.360
Your senior? That would make him my grand-professor!

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:45.130
Yet again, I meet a legendary pioneer of our field!

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:47.160
I'm unworthy of such joy!

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:50.330
Well, you must be Joseph.

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:51.900
You're exactly like I've heard.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:54.000
Though his talent is real.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.370
We'll stay up all through the night,

00:07:56.370 --> 00:08:00.010
breaking new ground and inventing incredible gadgets for science!

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:01.910
Someday, I'm sure.

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:05.680
Right now, investigating
Warp Particles and Babel comes first.

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:07.880
Ah, yes, you're right.

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:10.080
You've found yourself a great student.

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:16.270
What are you doing?

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:18.820
Demetrio...

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:19.920
Why are you here?

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:24.790
I saw a boy making a face that looked like he was lost.

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:27.400
I-I didn't make any face.

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:29.130
So? What are you doing?

00:09:32.270 --> 00:09:36.840
I was thinking how small this throne is.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:41.280
When Delzaine sat there, it seemed so much larger than that.

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:45.310
If no one sits on the throne, it's nothing more than a chair.

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:49.080
It's up to whoever sits there to make it what it is.

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:51.120
To whoever sits there...

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:55.820
The capital and castle are in ruins because the country itself is broken.

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:58.790
There's no one around to guide the kingdom or people.

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:02.800
This country needs a new king.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:08.800
That is, hopefully... one who rules better than Delzaine and Alzerm.

00:10:09.970 --> 00:10:11.370
I...

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:19.110
When it comes to Delzaine... and King Alzerm... I really know nothing.

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:22.480
I want to know. Who were they really?

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:24.450
I'm not running from the truth anymore.

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:31.860
Good idea. That's a step in the right direction.

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:34.390
I'll help you however I can.

00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:47.010
Why do I get stuck preparing the food?

00:10:47.010 --> 00:10:48.340
Oh, you're good!

00:10:48.340 --> 00:10:49.510
Hmm?!

00:10:49.510 --> 00:10:53.320
Deal with it. There's really no one left in the castle to cook.

00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:57.090
With all of us here now, they need all the help they can get.

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:58.490
So no whining.

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:04.230
Anyways, you're the newest in the Ignauts so that makes you the rookie.

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:06.230
Don't call me a rookie!

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:10.000
Besides, Guidoro and Gradido came after me.

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:11.900
I know! I'll make them do it!

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:12.870
Hmm?

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:14.900
Wait, no.

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:16.000
No!

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:20.540
It's creepy enough just thinking about them helping out in the kitchen!

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:23.170
Alicia? Do you have a minute?

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:28.520
Who are those people
Emilio brought back with him?

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:30.220
Well, uh...

00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:33.890
That's right! He met them all on his journey!

00:11:33.890 --> 00:11:39.230
They're like a volunteer army that helps people attacked by brigands and such.

00:11:39.230 --> 00:11:41.060
Those Zoozians, too?

00:11:41.060 --> 00:11:42.300
Yup.

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:46.440
Zoozians in a volunteer army?
They would do that sort of thing?

00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:47.870
Uh...

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:00.920
Oh? On a walk?

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:02.120
Yeah.

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:04.550
It's stifling being in the castle.

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:07.920
It seems we're not so welcome there.

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:09.660
I'm not that surprised.

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:12.460
Humans can't even get along with themselves.

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:16.400
With humans and Zoozians, the discord is even greater.

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:21.970
I hope the country can get rid of its hatred once it puts an end to this chaos.

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:23.840
That all depends on him...

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:27.340
Also...

00:12:27.340 --> 00:12:29.980
I sensed a strange presence in the forest.

00:12:29.980 --> 00:12:31.410
Me too...

00:12:54.470 --> 00:12:55.970
I knew it...

00:12:55.970 --> 00:13:01.480
Even in the south, the Warp Particles are severely declining.

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:04.980
The capital may be in danger.

00:13:04.980 --> 00:13:06.280
Why is that?

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:11.990
Unknown creatures are gathering in the forest near the castle.

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:13.390
What?

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:18.490
What are those monsters?

00:13:18.490 --> 00:13:20.330
We have too few to fight.

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:22.130
Should we just run away?

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:23.700
What are you talking about?!

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:27.540
If we don't stand and fight, who will defend the castle and capital?

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:30.640
We stand no chance!
We have too many injured!

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:36.510
Is it worth dying to protect the castle anymore? Or even the capital?

00:13:36.510 --> 00:13:40.070
If that's your attitude, we'll just have to take over.

00:13:42.520 --> 00:13:43.920
You...

00:13:46.150 --> 00:13:47.550
Let's move out!

00:13:50.690 --> 00:13:52.230
Zoozians...

00:13:52.230 --> 00:13:55.730
Zoozians fighting to help people?

00:13:55.730 --> 00:14:01.240
You've all fought long and hard protecting the city and castle.

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:02.770
Now it's our turn to fight.

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:05.410
Prince Emilio? You're fighting, too?

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:07.510
Please, don't! It's too dangerous!

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:11.210
I faced danger many times on my journey.

00:14:11.210 --> 00:14:13.580
Don't worry about us!

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:16.590
You might not think it, but we're pretty tough!

00:14:16.590 --> 00:14:21.720
Though Emilio always screws up and counts on me to save his ass.

00:14:21.720 --> 00:14:24.730
You've screwed up more times than I can even remember.

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:26.560
What? Say that again!

00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:30.130
Why don't you go back and help in the kitchen?

00:14:30.130 --> 00:14:32.230
It's not like you'll be any help here.

00:14:32.230 --> 00:14:35.600
Gah! You're a rotten prince with a filthy mouth.

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:38.540
Maybe you should just become a chef.

00:14:38.540 --> 00:14:41.240
After all, you're plain awful at fighting.

00:14:41.240 --> 00:14:43.810
I'm better than you! Want to fight and see?!

00:14:43.810 --> 00:14:45.210
With pleasure.

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:47.250
I already know that I'll win.

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:49.950
Hurry it up, you two! You're falling behind!

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:11.140
What a nasty bunch. What are these things?

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:14.310
It's Ibelda. Rather, his spawn.

00:15:14.310 --> 00:15:19.510
Your spear would make a perfect laundry hanger.
Why don't you go and dry some clothes?

00:15:19.510 --> 00:15:25.290
Hmph. Your sword is better at cutting through vegetables than it is cutting enemies.

00:15:25.290 --> 00:15:26.690
You're that bad.

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:28.120
Now you've said it!

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:30.620
Out of my way!

00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:39.160
This is bad. There's just too many.

00:15:50.810 --> 00:15:53.520
I could've done that myself.

00:15:53.520 --> 00:15:58.320
If you're that good, don't make it look like you need help.

00:15:58.320 --> 00:15:59.850
Guidoro's right.

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:01.290
Grr...

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:04.560
Shut up.

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:08.900
This scent...

00:16:09.700 --> 00:16:14.400
It's throbbing! Throbbing! Throbbing!

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:17.000
I know where you are, runts!

00:16:19.640 --> 00:16:21.840
How should I tear them apart?

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:27.350
I can't wait! I can't wait!
My wound is aching for fun!

00:16:27.350 --> 00:16:28.750
I see you...

00:16:37.730 --> 00:16:40.930
It's him! Ibelda!

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:43.200
I've been waiting for this, brats!

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:45.830
My wound is throbbing and it wants to have fun!

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:50.870
Over there?!

00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:55.340
Shun! Emilio!

00:17:02.780 --> 00:17:05.350
Throbbing! It's throbbing!

00:17:05.350 --> 00:17:08.220
What's with him?! He's gone nuts!

00:17:10.790 --> 00:17:12.230
Move it!

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:19.870
Emilio!

00:17:19.870 --> 00:17:21.800
Ibelda!

00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:27.030
Stay out of my way!

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:35.320
There's too many to handle!

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:37.420
This isn't good.

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:39.480
I'm done holding back!

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:57.300
This is trouble.

00:18:07.950 --> 00:18:10.420
Don't let them have all the fun!

00:18:10.420 --> 00:18:13.950
It's our duty to protect the castle and city!

00:18:26.470 --> 00:18:27.540
Don't push yourself.

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:31.840
Hmph. What can I hope to protect if I can't give it my all?

00:18:43.320 --> 00:18:46.820
Soldiers of the kingdom and
Zoozians fighting side by side...

00:18:46.820 --> 00:18:48.310
I could get used to this.

00:18:58.870 --> 00:18:59.700
We've got this!

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:01.140
Now!

00:19:07.510 --> 00:19:08.640
Not deep enough!

00:19:08.640 --> 00:19:11.840
Again?! You got me again?!

00:19:16.680 --> 00:19:18.180
Piece of cake.

00:19:21.690 --> 00:19:24.220
We saved the city!

00:19:25.690 --> 00:19:27.720
They made it through alive...

00:19:34.370 --> 00:19:36.240
I told you not to push yourself.

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:47.550
We did it!

00:19:47.550 --> 00:19:49.380
Protectors of the realm!

00:19:49.380 --> 00:19:51.950
We won! We really won!

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:54.960
I might have misjudged you.

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:59.690
Thank you. We won only because you all took the vanguard.

00:19:59.690 --> 00:20:02.130
You allowed our soldiers to band together.

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:04.290
Sorry for doubting you at first.

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:10.940
You were only doing your job and guarding the castle.

00:20:10.940 --> 00:20:12.410
No need to apologize.

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:18.410
Prince Emilio defeated the enemy leader!

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:19.150
He's a hero!

00:20:19.150 --> 00:20:21.050
Prince Emilio!

00:20:21.050 --> 00:20:22.080
S-Sure...

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:24.920
He's so strong now!

00:20:24.920 --> 00:20:27.320
Prince Emilio!

00:20:28.820 --> 00:20:32.260
Check out how awkward he is with all this attention.

00:20:37.430 --> 00:20:42.100
Will he be able to answer the trust they found in him?

00:20:42.100 --> 00:20:47.440
It's still only small, but I see him becoming a shining light for all.

00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:48.780
Or so I hope.

00:20:48.780 --> 00:20:51.300
That's one vision that would be good to see come true.

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:04.930
"To be continued..."

00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:13.800
<i>I've walked very far, so far</i>

00:21:13.800 --> 00:21:23.300
<i>And I'll walk even farther from here</i>

00:21:39.330 --> 00:21:46.070
<i>I don't wish for everything to stay the same</i>

00:21:46.070 --> 00:21:56.070
<i>Because change is what got me to where I am</i>

00:21:56.710 --> 00:22:05.250
<i>We've walked very far, so far</i>

00:22:05.250 --> 00:22:13.860
<i>We'll go farther than anyone's gone before</i>

00:22:13.860 --> 00:22:22.400
<i>Each of us can change the world</i>

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:31.570
<i>That's why I smile at you</i>
